From 4f5a1b36ed66e59c15868963322bf0f5cbf60b41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:08:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(xtask): share one job budget across the lanes of a
 gate wave

The release tier ran up to four lanes, each with -j 6 and
--test-threads=6: up to 24 compile jobs on a 6-job machine.

- budget.rs: one budget (default 6, CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS overrides).
- A wave of N lanes gives each lane budget/N jobs (minimum 1); a wave
  holds at most budget/2 lanes; a step alone keeps the full budget.
- The executor rewrites -j and --test-threads per step at run time, so
  the plan builders (and open PR #1952) stay unchanged.
- The gate prints the budget and the jobs of each wave, also in
  --dry-run.
- gate and runners skills: the sum of -j of all builds on one machine
  stays at or below its core count.

Fixes #2057

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
